# THE QIRAKI FILES — Points Economy, the Arithmetic (v4)

**ID:** PTS-MATH. **Tier:** 2, decision document. **Status:** RULED 2026-09-06. **Supersedes** Qiraki_Points_Economy_Math_v1 and the v2 rebuild of the same day.

**Changelog v3 (2026-09-06).** The Saturday question is ruled and the path boards are repriced against the gate rather than carried over from v1. Both changes below. **A finding worth stating first, because it is the more useful one:** the Saturday question was never actually open. Qiraki_Combat_Curriculum_Reference has carried "combat class runs Friday/Saturday only in Years 1-2, expands to Thursday-Saturday from Year 3 on" as a locked line for some time, and v1 of this document listed it as unresolved anyway. Nobody checked CBT. Worse, CBT's own version is contradicted by every delivered Year 1 chapter, which is Friday-only throughout, in narration and in dialogue. The ruling below fixes the doc rather than the chapters.

**On this rebuild, stated plainly rather than papered over.** A v2 of this file was written and is lost. This is a rebuild from v1 plus the author's ruling of 2026-09-06, not a recovery of it. The lost v2 was reported as correcting four defects; only one of those, the weapon-progression ladder, is recoverable from surviving material and is corrected in §5 below. If the other three surface again they will surface as new finds, and that is the honest state of it. Separately, Qiraki_Points_Economy_Audit_v1, named throughout v1 as this file's companion, is not in the project folder and has not been for at least three sessions.

## 1. The ruling

v1 ended by asking for gated or ungated. The answer is neither column on its own.

- **The four path boards are gated behind year-3 specialisation.** Meeps, Reeps, Tank, Munti. No cadet buys a path weapon, power unit or role equipment before choosing a path. Years 1 and 2 fight on issued gear.

- **The universal genetic and stimulant board is ungated.** Open from the first week of year one, to anybody, regardless of path or standing. Price alone rations it.

- **Combat class runs one day a week in Year 1, two from Year 2, three from Year 3.** Friday only, then Friday and Saturday, then Thursday to Saturday. Corrects CBT, which had Saturday running from Year 1 and was contradicted by every delivered Year 1 chapter.

- **Path prices are rederived against the Year 3 gate,** not carried from v1. v1's ungated column was priced against v1's own grade-by-year mapping, where E belonged to Year 2. Under the gate E belongs to Year 3, and v1's E price of 130,000 sat at a quarter of what a cadet has banked the day the gate opens, which gave the gate no bite at the one moment it is supposed to have all of it.

**Confirmed in delivered prose, B1.CH22.** Five boards on the combat-corridor wall, four paths and one narrower open board in the middle. Seven items on the open board. Cheapest 130, third one down 74,000, bottom of the board 76,000,000. Those four figures are on the page and are canon.

**What the gate does that pricing alone could not.** v1 §6 flagged the real cost of going ungated: the Year 1 cohort's uniform appearance on the field, which every delivered combat chapter has assumed, loses its explanation. The path gate restores it and does it better than a grade rule would. Nobody in years 1 and 2 can buy a weapon at any price, so the cohort looks identical on the field regardless of what any individual has banked, and the difference between a cadet with fourteen thousand and a cadet with four hundred is invisible until the year everybody chooses.

**What the gate deliberately does not do.** It does not gate grade. Once a cadet has a path in year 3, every grade on that board is open and price is the only constraint. The snowball lock survives intact: two cadets who specialise the same week walk out with different kit, and the gap widens from there.

## 2. The model

Unchanged from v1 and re-verified against delivered prose this pass. Every parameter is either locked in Qiraki_Weapons_And_Progression or forced by a number already on the page.

| Parameter | Value | Where it comes from |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Combat points per win | 20 x month index | LOCKED table |
| Class activity per success | 10 x month index | LOCKED table |
| Baseline per graded item | 1 x month index | LOCKED table |
| Combat sessions per month, Y1 | 4 | Friday only, every delivered chapter |
| Combat sessions per month, Y2 | 8 | Friday and Saturday, ruled 2026-09-06 |
| Combat sessions per month, Y3-7 | 12 | Thursday to Saturday, CBT's own schedule |
| Wins per Friday, Year 1 | 3, 5, 6, 8, 11, 15, 17, 18, 19, 20, 20, 20 | Fitted. Ch.18 puts Corw at 11 in May, Ch.21 puts Trav at 19 in June |
| Wins per session, Y2 onward | 20 | Plateau, opponents scale with him |
| Graded class successes per month | 8 | Fitted |
| Graded baseline items per month | 20 | Fitted |

**Monthly income formula:** month m with s sessions and w wins per session yields **m x (20sw + 100)**. Year 1 is s = 4, Year 2 is s = 8, Years 3 to 7 are s = 12. The 100 is class activity and graded baseline, which do not scale with combat days and are the reason Year 2 does not simply double.

**Fit against the page, four independent figures from four chapters.**

| Figure | Modelled | Delivered | Source |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Trav, mid-June Y1 | 14,680 | 14,640 | B1.CH21 |
| Corw, year to date, 21 June | 16,790 | 16,500 | B1.CH21, B1.CH22 |
| Corw, early March | 2,100 | 2,140 | B1.CH11 |
| Corw, one Friday in May | 1,100 | 1,100 | B1.CH18 |

